  "limits": "Context instances retain the selected immutable Cell plan, not a separate root/tail identity. Endpoints and read tables come from compiled instructions, eliminating runtime source Rule lookup/cloning. Version equality reads the current graph directly; only an invalidated scope refreshes its existing snapshot allocation. Plan switches discard old state, while exact root/read leases and canonical-literal union resets remain. The added shared plan reference is retained until this cache is dropped or switched. Existing counters do not measure metadata bytes or removed temporary allocations; no speed claim and no full cache/index takeover.",
